{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBSRL2jLwDF5pch358JM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 5** (Ag 0.50 / Sb 0.50) as the best composition. At 0.369%, its EQE was the highest of the three I measured. All 3 EQE measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD measurements are used.\n\n| Index | Ag : Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3 | 0.57 : 0.43 | 0.330 |\n| **5** | **0.50 : 0.50** | **0.369** |\n| 9 | 0.36 : 0.64 | 0.161 |\n\n- **Where the best composition is:** EQE drops on both sides of the 1:1 composition. So the best spot is probably between indices 3 and 7. Index 4 (0.54 : 0.46) is the obvious untested neighbour, but I had no budget left to check it.\n- **What the X-ray scans showed:** Samples richer in silver (index 1) are mostly metallic silver. Samples richer in antimony (indices 9 and 13) are mostly the pyrochlore AgSbO3 phase, with the lattice getting slightly larger toward the antimony end. Index 5 is a mix of phases. The pyrochlore-rich sample 9 scored well below index 5, so the pyrochlore phase alone doesn't explain the best result. I identified these phases by matching peak positions by hand, so treat them as likely rather than certain.\n- **What I ruled out:** I skipped measuring index 13 because it looks structurally like index 9 and the EQE was falling toward the antimony end. I skipped index 1 because its scan is mostly silver metal and the EQE was already dropping at index 3."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":595,"cache_read_input_tokens":9502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":595},"output_tokens":544,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"684b0fd7-0e78-495d-b239-bf789284d9ab","uuid":"5d596987-cd33-47c